.TH RETA\-MOJO\-COMPAT 1 "July 2026" "reta_arch_mojo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reta\-mojo\-compat \- public compatibility frontend for Mojo/Python bridge checks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reta\-mojo\-compat
.RI [ ARGUMENT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reta\-mojo\-compat
runs the Mojo/Python compatibility frontend. It keeps explicit compatibility and reference\-boundary checks separate from the normal user commands.

.SH NOTES
This command is installed because it is a build or diagnostic target of the native Mojo port. Normal users usually start with .BR reta (1), .BR rp (1), .BR rpl (1), .BR rpe (1), or .BR rpb (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and non-zero on errors, failed checks, missing build targets, or invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reta(1), rp(1), rpl(1), rpe(1), rpb(1), reta-mojo(1)
